# Population Genetics Simulated with Playing Cards

**Authors:** Oliver, P. T. P.

## Abstract
Describes how to use playing cards as simulators to demonstrate several aspects of allelism and allele frequency in a gene pool. They provide an &quot;unexpected&quot; result, promote group discussion and may stimulate students to devise variations for comparison. (BR)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ121621

